[SECTION]
TITLE: Document Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This Software Verification Plan describes the verification strategy and procedures used to satisfy the verification objectives for Design Assurance Level A software. It establishes the approach for demonstrating that the software requirements are satisfied and that the software does not contain errors.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1. Organization and Independence

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.1 Development Organization

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The software development organization is the Flight Systems Engineering Department of Avionics Systems Inc., responsible for requirements analysis, design, and implementation.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.2 Verification Organization

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The software verification organization is the Independent Verification and Validation (IV&V) Group, which reports to the Quality Assurance Director independently of the development organization.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 1.3 Independence

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Independence requirements for Level A software are met through organizational separation. The verification team has no reporting relationship to the development team and has independent budget and schedule authority. Reviews, test case development, and test execution are performed by verification personnel who did not develop the item under test.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2. Verification Methods

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.1 Reviews

[PLAN]
UID: SVP-METHOD-001
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Reviews are inspection activities performed to verify that software artifacts comply with standards and requirements. Reviews include requirements reviews, design reviews, code reviews, and test procedure reviews. Formal review checklists based on DO-178C objectives will be used.

**Applicability:** Applied to all software requirements, design, code, and verification procedures.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.2 Analysis

[PLAN]
UID: SVP-METHOD-002
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Analysis includes examination of software artifacts to verify properties that cannot be easily verified through testing. Analysis methods include:
- Requirements traceability analysis
- Data and control flow analysis
- Timing and memory analysis
- Stack usage analysis
- Structural coverage analysis (MC/DC for Level A)
- Worst-case execution time (WCET) analysis

**Applicability:** Applied to requirements, design, code, and verification coverage.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.3 Test

[PLAN]
UID: SVP-METHOD-003
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Testing exercises the software with inputs to verify correct behavior and outputs. Test levels include:
- Requirements-based testing (high-level tests)
- Low-level testing (unit and integration tests)
- Software/hardware integration testing
- Robustness testing (error handling and boundary conditions)

**Applicability:** Applied to verify all software requirements at appropriate abstraction levels.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.4 Demonstration

[PLAN]
UID: SVP-METHOD-004
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Demonstration verifies operational characteristics through execution in the target environment. Used for features that require human observation or specific operational scenarios.

**Applicability:** Applied selectively for user interface and operational features.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 2.5 Inspection

[PLAN]
UID: SVP-METHOD-005
LEVEL: A
STATEMENT: >>>
Inspection is detailed visual examination of software artifacts. Used for aspects that cannot be effectively verified through automated means.

**Applicability:** Applied to build procedures, configuration data, and final object code.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3. Verification Environment

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.1 Environment Description

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The verification environment consists of:
- Target hardware (Flight Management Computer) with JTAG debug interface
- Hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) simulator for sensor and avionics interfaces
- Software development workstations (Linux-based)
- Requirements management system with traceability tools
- Static analysis tools for code quality and coverage
- Version control and configuration management system
- Automated test execution framework
- Coverage analysis tools (structural coverage for MC/DC)
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: 3.2 Hardware

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
- Flight Management Computer (target hardware)
- Hardware-in-the-loop simulator with aircraft sensor models
- Control Display Unit (CDU) interface
- JTAG debugger and trace analyzer
<<<

[/SECTION]

